**/secret**

pi/agent/auth.json
pi/agent/sessions
pi/agent/settings.json
pi/agent/sessions.json
pi/agent/mcp-cache.json
pi/agent/mcp-npx-cache.json
pi/agent/bin
pi/agent/cache


/pi/context-mode/sessions
/pi/context-mode/content
/pi/agent/trust.json
/pi/agent/skills/**/*.env*

# orca (~/.orca) — same shape as pi: the real dir is symlinked to orca/ in the
# repo, so orca's generated state lands there too. Only keybindings.json is worth
# tracking. agent-hooks/ is regenerated by the Agent status hooks setting.
# ~/.config/orca is Electron app data (private E2EE keypair, runtime token,
# cookies, sqlite) and is never symlinked or tracked — see orca/README.md.
orca/agent-hooks/
# Encrypted API keys the app writes next to its config (e.g. opencode-go) — never tracked.
orca/*.enc

# Claude Code (~/.claude) — track config only, ignore runtime + secrets.
# Whitelist approach: ignore everything, then re-include the config we manage.
claude/*
!claude/settings.json
!claude/keybindings.json
!claude/CLAUDE.md
!claude/hooks/
!claude/commands/
!claude/agents/
!claude/skills/
# plugins/ holds only machine-specific runtime state (cache, clones, install paths).
# Reproducibility comes from settings.json: extraKnownMarketplaces + enabledPlugins
# auto-install everything on startup. So plugins/ stays fully ignored.

# Herdr (~/.config/herdr) — track config only, ignore runtime.
# Only herdr/config.toml is symlinked; the rest of ~/.config/herdr stays local
# (session.json, sockets, logs, plugin lock are machine-local runtime state).
herdr/*.log
herdr/*.sock
herdr/session.json
herdr/.plugins.lock
herdr/agent-detection/

# IntelliJ — track config only, ignore machine-local state.
# Unlike claude/ and pi/, the whole IntelliJ config dir CANNOT be symlinked
# (version-specific path, machine state mixed with config). Settings Sync
# handles cross-machine sync for keymaps/codestyles/options. The dotfiles
# repo tracks only .ideavimrc (symlinked to ~/.ideavimrc) and reference
# copies of keymaps for version history.
intellij/*
!intellij/ideavimrc
!intellij/keymaps/
!intellij/MIGRATION-ADVISORY.md
/pi/pi-acp/session-map.json
/pi/agent/settings.json
/pi/agent/models-store.json
/pi/agent/run-history.jsonl
pi/agent/missions/
# pi-subagents extension runtime state (last-seen-version.json etc.)
pi/agent/pi-subagents/

pi/agent/.skill-lock.json

# Nix / Home Manager build output symlinks
/result
/result-*

# Agent skills — version the docs (SKILL.md + references/ + scripts) so a fresh
# machine gets working skills. Secrets and runtime stay local: .env* under
# pi/agent/skills/ is ignored above, .skill-lock.json below.
# claude/skills/* are symlinks into pi/agent/skills — tracked so the links survive.
# These docs name the client services the agent works on, so they are exempted
# from scripts/check-identifiers.sh; they carry no credentials.
